  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "QCS-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "The quotient character encodes the obstruction to extending a fixed character",
      "anchor": "inputs-quadratic-character-extension",
      "statement": "Let U be relatively open of index two in V, with coset representative σ outside U. The fixed locally constant additive 𝔽₂-characters on U vanishing on S∩U admit an injection into the corresponding character space on V when S∩V⊆U. An invariant character extends precisely when its value on σ² is zero.",
      "hypotheses": "Γ a topological group, U≤V≤Γ, [V:U]=2, S⊆Γ. Fixed means φ(σ⁻¹uσ)=φ(u) for every u∈U. Stability of S under conjugation by V is assumed in the full square theorem; the injection on the fixed subset needs only S∩V⊆U.",
      "definitions": [
        "C(H) consists of locally constant homomorphisms H→(𝔽₂,+) vanishing on S∩H.",
        "b(φ)=φ(σ²). If any b is nonzero, choose one fixed φ₀ of value one; otherwise choose φ₀=0.",
        "For χ fixed with χ(σ²)=0, Eχ(v)=χ(v) on U and χ(vσ) off U. ε is the character of V/U with ε(σ)=1."
      ],
